so there has been reports that may the  12th is the date that finland will  decide to apply to nato is that right  well that date is important  and thank you for having me in the  program  the president of finland has said that  by the may 12th he will make his opinion  public we started this democratic  process almost immediately after  after the russian invasion of ukraine  and it has been a very  thorough parliamentary procedure with a  report from the government to the  parliament on the options  and  indeed applying for nato membership is  one of the options so on the 12th  things are moving they have been moving  of course already before that with  various political parties stating their  opinions and all indeed mps we have 200  members of parliament coming out to the  public and saying openly what they  think about it  you've obviously never felt the need to  apply to join nato before  what's changed  i have to go a little bit back on  history actually almost a thousand years  we were part of the swedish kingdom for  six centuries then we were part of the  russian empire as an  as an um very autonomous um grand duchy  so we have throughout  all of our history being between east  and the west and finland has often been  sort of dragged into conflicts that we  had very little  ownership of that that had very little  to do with finland but more with the big  power politics  and that is why the finns have had a  very pragmatic approach to military  alignment we haven't seen it as a  necessity necessity we might have been  even suspicious about it but now with  the  invasion of ukraine by russia which we  completely completely condemn and which  the finnish population doesn't  understand at all and doesn't accept  the the climate the political climate  and the popular opinion has changed  um this week your foreign ministry has  said a russian army helicopter violated  finland's airspace how concerned are you  about  aggression from russia  when it comes to violations of airspace  we have had plenty of those before  during the past years when we always  react to them and we demand an  explanation  um that is not new we are also quite  prepared for any other type of  influence or influence attempts from  russia during the process of application  if we do to decide to start it  we have  invested in our preparedness and i don't  mean only defense  but the sort of whole of society  approach comprehensive security for  decades and i think we are quite well  prepared for different types of uh  influence including cyber hybrid or  indeed uh violations of our territory  there's obviously a border between  finland and russia we've all seen the  atrocities that have happened  in ukraine  frankly if you're not a member of nato  is finland feeling vulnerable  i wouldn't say vulnerable is the word we  are concerned we are very concerned for  the security structure of europe that we  have built our security around  but as i said we have been investing in  our own national defense for decades we  have quite a robust  defense force both the army the air  force and the navy so in that sense we  are not  overly  worried  what we are concerned about is what this  this attack and this war will mean to  the european security structure in the  future and therefore we have taken this  uh opportunity to consider our route  forward and we shall see where where the  parliamentary and the democratic  decisions lead us  are you confident that if you did apply  to join nato that you would be accepted  reports that the croatian president  saying that he would actually veto  any application  we are following very carefully the  discussion in different major countries  and and embassies including my own have  been tasked to find out what the  political climate in each and every  member state is for the part of the uk i  can say  and that was also uh repeated by tom  tuggenheim just a couple of minutes ago  that uh the british support is very  clear so we have absolutely no no  concerns about about britain whatsoever  each member states and there are 30 of  those in nato is a case of its own and  of course we are looking at each and  every one of them but at the moment i  wouldn't say that we have particular  concerns of any of them  what are you prepared to contribute to  nato if you were to become members  certainly we take our memberships in in  any organization very seriously since  other a rule away nation and a country  we have a strong national defense so i  think our inclusion in nato would  strengthen  the security situation around the baltic  sea  we are also extremely solid democracy uh  the least corrupt country in the world  um and in some fields of technology  including  mobile networks  intelligence quantum intelligence we are  ahead of the field you might say so i  think we have a lot lots to contribute  and just finally obviously the  importance of nato has really been  highlighted with the war in ukraine but  there has been criticism of nato  previously uh by many different um  people of course um that it's too  aggressive that it's provoked russia by  moving troops do you accept any of those  criticisms of how nato has been i think  we see nato as a defense alliance and  and  of course when you plan for defence you  have to  prepare for different alternatives but i  don't think  we uh see in finland see that nato uh  and indeed nato member states can be in  any way blamed  for what has happened in ukraine that  was a russian aggression against a  sovereign neighboring state uh and  completely unwarranted and unquote
 

